<title>MEXICO: Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 25.71 pct in auction.</title>
<headline>Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate 25.71 pct in auction.</headline>
<text>
<p>MEXICO CITY, Dec 30 - Mexico's 28-day Cetes rate fell in this week's primary auction and demand fell, Banco de Mexico said.</p>
<p>Auction results were: (all rates in percent)</p>
<p>Maturity    Weighted Avg   Change (bps)  Min Rate  Max Rate</p>
<p>28-Day	25.71	    -154	    25.65     25.75</p>
<p>91-Day	25.99	    -56	     25.84     26.11</p>
<p>182-Day     25.64	    -4		25.50     25.76</p>
<p>363-Day     25.98				25.49     26.10</p>
<p>Last week the 343-day paper was assigned at 25.75 pct.  </p>
<p>Maturity    Assigned	  Demand		Bid/Cover</p>
<p>28-Day	900 million pesos   2.95 bln pesos     3.28</p>
<p>91-Day	900 million pesos   3.37 bln pesos     3.74</p>
<p>182 Day     900 million pesos   2.38 bln pesos     2.64</p>
<p>363-Day     600 million pesos   1.45 bln pesos     2.42</p>
<p>The bid-to-cover ratio for the auction as a whole was 3.08 compared to 3.25 the week before, on demand of 10.75 billion pesos the week before.  </p>
<p>Tails were as follows:</p>
<p>    28-Day			    4 basis points</p>
<p>    91-Day			   12 basis points</p>
<p>    182-Day			  12 basis points</p>
<p>    363-Day			  12 basis points</p>
<p>((-- Mexico City newsroom, 525 728-9507))</p>
</text>
